.Dd September 22, 2026
.Dt PASSWD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm passwd
.Nd change a user's password
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl d
.Op Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
changes the password of
.Ar user ,
or of the caller when no user is given.
.Pp
On NextBSD an account lives in one of two places, and
.Nm
edits whichever holds it:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Proper users are records in
.Pa Users.plist
under
.Pa /Local/Library/DirectoryServices
.Po
or
.Pa /Network/Library/DirectoryServices
on a machine joined to a directory server
.Pc .
Their password is the
.Va passwordHash
field, an SHA-512
.Xr crypt 3
hash in the form Gershwin uses.
.It
Root and the system users are in
.Pa /etc/master.passwd .
Their hash is rewritten there and
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8
is run, as on FreeBSD.
.El
.Pp
A user changes their own password after typing the old one; root sets
anyone's without it.
On a joined client the accounts in use are the server's and
.Nm
refuses to edit them; change the password on the server.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d
Remove the password of a directory user, so they log in without one
.Po
the record's
.Va noPassword
flag
.Pc .
Root only.
.It Fl l
Accepted for compatibility; every password is local.
.El
.Pp
When standard input is not a terminal, the passwords are read from it
one per line, the old one first when it is required.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/Network/Library/DirectoryServices/Users.plist" -compact
.It Pa /Local/Library/DirectoryServices/Users.plist
directory users
.It Pa /Network/Library/DirectoryServices/Users.plist
the server's users, when joined
.It Pa /etc/master.passwd
root and the system users
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr chpass 1 ,
.Xr crypt 3 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr dscli 8 ,
.Xr pw 8 ,
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8 ,
.Xr vipw 8
.Sh HISTORY
This
.Nm
replaced FreeBSD's on NextBSD when user accounts moved to the
DirectoryServices plists.
NIS is not supported;
.Nm yppasswd
says so.
